# dotfiles-Alpine/.gitignore
*.log
*.bak
*.pre-dotfiles.*
.DS_Store
# Crash dumps. `core.[0-9]*` and NOT `core.*`: this repo tracks core.lock, and Core itself
# tracks core.manifest and core.version — a blanket rule would hide the next such file the
# moment someone added one, silently. Bare `core` is deliberately not matched either: that
# is the vendored Core DIRECTORY. Matches the kernel/glibc `core.<pid>` spelling.
core.[0-9]*
# host-local zsh fragment (v4 name; blib_migrate_v4 renamed the pre-v4 zsh/local.zsh)
zsh/99-local.zsh
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# private SSH material — deny-by-default, and nothing here is tracked any more.
# The ssh CLIENT CONFIG moved into Core (dotgibson/dotfiles-core#450): it is now
# core/ssh/config, symlinked by blib_link_core. Keep this rule: it means a key
# dropped under ssh/ is untracked unless someone deliberately allowlists it, which
# is the safe direction to be wrong in. An OS-specific ssh need is ssh/os.conf
# (linked to ~/.ssh/config.d/50-os.conf) and would need its own ! line here.
ssh/*
